  /* ======================= ONLINE PLAY: each player on their own device =======================
   * The host's browser is the referee. It runs the game and keeps a numbered log of every command that changes it
   * (start the auction, bid, pass, clock ran out, next lot, kick off, play it out, transfer, final whistle).
   * Every other browser replays exactly the same commands on the same seeded game, so all screens show the same auction.
   * A player's tap is sent to the host, checked (their own seat, same lot, same price) and only then played and broadcast.
   * Someone who joins late or reconnects gets the whole log and catches up instantly. */
